        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_35_02_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_35",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_35_02",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That reads more like an implementation plan than a user story — it's written from the developer's perspective and already specifies the column, the method name, and the route. A user story should describe the need from the *user's* point of view and the value it delivers, leaving the \"how\" open: something like \"As a forum member, I want to mark a topic as unread so I can easily find it again later.\" The implementation details you listed are great, but they belong in the ticket's technical notes or a design doc attached to the story, not in the story itself."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_35_02_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_35",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_35_02",
          "type": "step-finish",
          "reason": "stop",
          "cost": 0.01,
          "tokens": {
            "input": 1200,
            "output": 320,
            "reasoning": 0,
            "cache": {
              "read": 0,
              "write": 0
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "info": {
        "id": "msg_ses_35_03",
        "sessionID": "ses_35",
        "role": "user",
        "time": {
          "created": 1759320007600
        },
        "agent": "build",
        "model": {
          "providerID": "anthropic",
          "modelID": "claude-sonnet-5"
        }
      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_35_03_01",
          "sessionID": "ses_35",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_35_03",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Hmm, I see what you mean, but if I don't specify the exact function names and the route and all that, how is whoever picks up the ticket supposed to know what to build? Isn't that just leaving it vague and making more work for them to figure out on their own?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "info": {
        "id": "msg_ses_35_04",
        "sessionID": "ses_35",
        "role": "assistant",
        "time": {
          "created": 1759320008600,
          "completed": 1759320009200
        },
        "parentID": "msg_ses_35_03",
        "modelID": "claude-sonnet-5",
        "providerID": "anthropic",
        "mode": "build",
        "agent": "build",
        "path": {
          "cwd": "/home/student/nodebb",
          "root": "/home/student/nodebb"
        },
        "cost": 0.01,
        "tokens": {
          "input": 1200,
          "output": 320,
          "reasoning": 0,
          "cache": {
            "read": 0,
            "write": 0
          }
        }
      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_35_04_01",
          "sessionID": "ses_35",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_35_04",
          "type": "step-start"
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_35_04_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_35",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_35_04",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That's a fair worry, but it's solved by splitting the two concerns rather than merging them: the user story stays at the behavioral level (\"what the user can now do and why\"), and you add acceptance criteria underneath it — \"a topic with `unread: true` shows a badge in the topic list,\" \"marking unread persists across reload\" — which describe observable behavior, not code. The actual column name, method signature, and route are design decisions the implementer (maybe you!) makes afterward, during implementation, not requirements the story has to lock in up front. Separating them means the story stays valid even if the implementation changes later."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_35_04_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_35",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_35_04",
          "type": "step-finish",
          "reason": "stop",
          "cost": 0.01,
          "tokens": {
            "input": 1200,
            "output": 320,
            "reasoning": 0,
            "cache": {
              "read": 0,
              "write": 0
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
